00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.400
So now you can see the reactionís really
going and itís really exothermic,

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.210
weíre forming aluminium triiodide, and the
exotherm is actually heating

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.680
and starting to sublime off the excess iodine
which you can see coming

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.369
off as this really nice purple plume.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:22.490
Iodine is this beautifully-coloured element.
It has this beautiful purple

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:28.619
colour. If you put it in solution, the colour
of the solution varies

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.430
depending what you dissolve it in. If you
dissolve it in water, itís a sort-of

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.829
dirty brown colour. If you dissolve it in
an organic material like

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:43.930
chloroform or carbon tetrachloride it is a
beautiful purple colour.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.649
Iodine is halide, a halogen element from the
far right-hand side of the

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:54.010
periodic table and it's strongly oxidising
in nature. Likes to nick electrons

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:58.770
off other atoms, so what weíre going to do
is we are going to do a

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:02.350
reaction with iodine, and today weíve ground
some iodine. So itís

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:08.100
normally found from chemical suppliers as
really nice large crystals. But

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.580
what we want to do as a reaction with it,
well we need to make sure that

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:15.610
the surface area of the iodine is really,
really large so that all of it can

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.330
react very very quickly with the other component.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:23.939
Iodine also occurs quite widely in nature
and is absolutely essential to

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:29.560
life. If you donít have iodine, your thyroid
gland, which is a small gland

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.960
that controls development of all sorts of
things in your body, doesnít

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:42.100
operate properly. Nowadays, iodide is added
to table salt in countries like

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.920
the UK and most other developed countries
so nearly everybody has

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:51.930
enough iodine. In the old days iodine had
to be got from the

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:56.450
environment and usually from the spray from
the sea that was blown

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:02.200
across the land, and so in Nottingham, which
is really near the centre of

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.500
England a long way from the sea, or relatively
long way from the sea,

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:12.599
there were serious illnesses caused by people
not having enough iodine.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:18.959
So-called goiter, which caused a swelling,
the thyroid gland gets bigger,

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:25.409
and this used to be called Derbyshire neck
this unpleasant illness,

00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:29.189
because it happened in this area of Nottingham
and Derbyshire.

00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:31.519
So what weíre going to do is that we are
going to mix it now with

00:02:31.519 --> 00:02:35.739
another element and that element is aluminium.
So aluminium has

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:39.430
electrons to give away. Iodineís gonna nab
ëem. Going to see some

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:43.290
oxidation chemistry in the formation of a
new compound, which is

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.420
aluminium triiodide. Itís a really nice chemical
reaction. But the way that

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.480
we do it is that we mix the two together and
we have to add water which

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.890
acts a bit like solvent and also the oxygen
in the water activates the

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:58.349
iodine so that it becomes more strongly oxidising
and then hopefully weíll

00:02:58.349 --> 00:03:01.519
see the new reaction. So Iím going to just
put some out into this small

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:03.939
vessel.

00:03:03.939 --> 00:03:08.299
You can see this development effect of iodine
really well that if you had

00:03:08.299 --> 00:03:15.799
tadpoles, baby frogs, they donít develop
their legs and turn into frogs

00:03:15.799 --> 00:03:17.839
unless there is iodine in the water.

00:03:17.839 --> 00:03:22.529
The other component in this reaction is aluminium,
ok; and weíre using

00:03:22.529 --> 00:03:26.089
very, very finely powdered aluminium. Not
foil or not a rather large

00:03:26.089 --> 00:03:29.389
lump. This has been especially powdered for
us, so again it has a very,

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:31.510
very high surface area.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:36.659
One of my favourite chemical equations is
ëtadpoles plus iodine goes to

00:03:36.659 --> 00:03:41.209
frogsí. So you can see the aluminium and
the iodine mixed within this

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:47.900
solid mixture. Now still, these two components,
these two elements they

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:51.299
are still held away from one another they
canít react. So what we need

00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:54.549
to do is add a small amount of water, which
actually acts like a solvent

00:03:54.549 --> 00:03:57.529
but actually activates the iodine and then
weíll wait and see what

00:03:57.529 --> 00:03:59.290
happens with the chemical reaction.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:04.879
Iodine can be used as a disinfectant, in fact
chlorine can be as well, but

00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:10.159
solution of iodine is often used when people
have cuts. So if you cut

00:04:10.159 --> 00:04:14.249
yourself, fortunately I havenít any cuts
at the moment, you can paint on

00:04:14.249 --> 00:04:19.829
iodine and because of its rather red colour
it made cuts often look much

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:23.479
worse. Children would come home from school
and their whole hand

00:04:23.479 --> 00:04:28.430
would be red and this would cause some excitement
at home but it is

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:31.270
quite an effective antiseptic.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:36.930
Water: just take a small amount and add it
to the reaction. So you can

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:39.880
see itís starting to go now the chemical
reaction because we are seeing

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:44.030
the excess iodine subliming in the form of
a vapour. Now if we go in

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:48.310
close we can hear it fizzing because this
is actually an oxidation reaction

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:54.110
and the formation of the new aluminium triiodide.
Now Iím going to just

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:58.490
mix this slightly to try and increase the
rate of the chemical reaction

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:03.150
slightly. So now you can see the reactionís
really going and itís really

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.630
exothermic, weíre forming aluminium triiodide,
and the exotherm is

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.509
actually heating and starting to sublime off
the excess iodine which you

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:15.849
can see coming off as this really nice purple
plume. Now deep inside the

00:05:15.849 --> 00:05:19.199
reaction now you can see the exothermic or
the energy coming out and

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:22.879
starting to cause a flame. Really, really
nice, really rapid chemical

00:05:22.879 --> 00:05:28.909
reaction: really beautiful. So weíre forming
aluminium triiodide here

00:05:28.909 --> 00:05:33.030
which again is a very, very delicate compound;
quite reactive in itself.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:38.900
So you can see now the really nice new crystalline
material. So, sadly,

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.401
